{"name":"Grey Pinstripe","hex":"#4e4e52","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"pinstripe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very thin stripe on a fabric or other surface.","A fabric decorated with such stripes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pinstripe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pinstripes","blocks":[{"text":"Pinstripes are a pattern of very thin stripes of any color running in parallel. The pattern is often found in fashion fabrics. Pinstripes are very thin, often 1⁄30 inch (0.85 mm) in width, and are created with one single-warp yarn."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Pinstripe.jpg/330px-Pinstripe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinstripes","wikidata":"Q3247883"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Portrait_of_Sir_Henry_Dale_Wellcome_M0017462.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Sir_Henry_Dale_Wellcome_M0017462.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Portrait_of_Sir_Henry_Da